# THE ONE THAT ACTUALLY APPLIES.
#
# docs/DEPLOY.md recommends setting Vercel's Root Directory to `game`. Vercel reads
# .vercelignore from the root of the PROJECT, not of the repository — so with that
# setting the .vercelignore at the repo root is never read at all. The root one stays
# for the other case (Root Directory left unset, where the repo root IS the project).
#
# THIS FILE IS NOW EMPTY OF RULES, and that is the point. It used to carry four globs
# excluding source art that lived inside this folder:
#
#   assets/GIF               3 delivered GIFs                   7.6MB
#   assets/char/*-gif.png    un-sliced character sheets         9.8MB
#   assets/option-shape/*.png the delivered blocks              23MB
#   assets/art/cover.png     the cover render                   2.5MB
#
# 43MB of build inputs that no URL in the game ever requests, sitting in the folder
# that gets uploaded, kept off the CDN only by these globs being correct in two
# separate files. Any new source file dropped in the wrong folder shipped silently.
#
# All of it now lives in art-source/ instead, which is outside this folder entirely,
# so there is nothing here to exclude: game/ contains only what the game loads. The
# tools that consume the source art read it from art-source/ (see
# tools/build-option-shapes.mjs, slice-char.mjs, gif-to-grid.mjs, assets.mjs).
#
# Keep it that way. If something in here needs excluding, that is the signal it is in
# the wrong folder.
